{"uid":"progs/src/lxsecc.c::_GNU_SOURCE","name":"_GNU_SOURCE","qualname":"_GNU_SOURCE","kind":"macro","file":"progs/src/lxsecc.c","line":13,"end_line":13,"language":"c","signature":"#define _GNU_SOURCE","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"lxsecc.c - Linux seccomp-bpf, prctl and /proc/self/exe probe (FreeDom readiness step 5, docs/spec/kernel.md \"Linux seccomp-bpf, prctl and /proc/self/exe\").","description":"Exercises exactly what FreeDom's tab worker relies on: re-exec through\n/proc/self/exe, no_new_privs, the dumpable flag, and a seccomp filter whose\nallowlist, ERRNO and KILL actions, W^X argument check, inheritance across\nfork, stacking and strict mode all behave like Linux. Every filter is\ninstalled in a forked child so the probe itself stays unconfined. Prints\n\"lxsecc: <check> ok\" or \"lxsecc: <check> FAIL <detail>\", then \"lxsecc: all\nok\" with exit 0, or \"lxsecc: <n> failed\" with exit 1.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"progs/src/lxsecc.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
